--TEST--
A reply a test's answer table served with no `tls` session reports none, whichever scheme its URL wrote, and every `Core\Http\TlsInfo` member sits behind the one check that answer forces — `rule:http-server/a-reply-reports-its-tls-session`, `rule:testing/an-outbound-call-is-answered-from-a-table`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Http\Response::tls
// The claim is *an edge*: an outbound call in a test ends at the answer table,
// and an answer registered with no `tls` session reports none, so `tls()` is
// `null` — for an `https` URL exactly as for an `http` one, because neither of
// them reached a socket. `http-response-tls-reports-the-session-a-test-described.nvst`
// is the answer that names one.
Core\Test::answerHttp("https://api.example.com/secure", 200, {body: "ok"});
Core\Test::answerHttp("http://api.example.com/plain", 200, {body: "ok"});

var $secure = Core\Http\Client::get("https://api.example.com/secure");
var $plain = Core\Http\Client::get("http://api.example.com/plain");

echo $secure->status(), " ", $secure->tls() != null ? "session" : "no session", "\n";
echo $plain->status(), " ", $plain->tls() != null ? "session" : "no session", "\n";

// The seven members of `Core\Http\TlsInfo` are what a reply that did arrive
// over TLS answers, and the answer being `?Core\Http\TlsInfo` is what makes the
// check above the only way to reach them. The branch is written and never runs
// here: that it compiles is the surface, that it is skipped is the table's
// answer.
var $info = $secure->tls();
if ($info != null) {
    echo $info->version(), " ", $info->cipher(), "\n";
    echo $info->verified() ? "verified" : "relaxed", "\n";
    echo Core\Arr::count($info->peerChain()), "\n";
    echo $info->subject(), " ", $info->issuer(), "\n";
    echo $info->expiry()->toIso(), "\n";
}

// The rest of the reply is unaffected by having no session to report: a table
// answers a body and a status like any origin, and only the session is absent.
echo $secure->text(), " ", $plain->text(), "\n";
--EXPECT--
200 no session
200 no session
ok ok
